[ceiling] These are the roofs of the two side-entry M5 square-nut pockets at print Z11.8, above their Z7.6 floors. The 4.2 mm pocket height accepts the stocked 4 mm nuts. Each pocket retains a 3.2 mm roof and a 7.6 mm preload-bearing floor, with a diameter-5.5 mm screw passage. The native Tree(auto)/default slice supplies two bed-rooted supports with interfaces at Z11.00–11.24 beneath the roofs, recorded in ready/tube-insertion-centered-grip-petgf-left04-z004-mark2.support-audit.json. The side entries provide removal access before nut loading and carrier assembly. Physical removal effort and printed load capacity remain unmeasured.
alternatives: An open mating-face pocket removes the roof and adds an opening at the rigid closure face. A sloping roof reduces the rectangular nut height clearance. Opening the underside removes the floor that receives screw preload. The supported flat chamber preserves the stocked nut's capture and bearing surfaces.
